; NULLWORD object regression probe.
;
; WHATO leaves 255 (NULLWORD) in flag 51 when nothing matched, so an
; indirected condact legally arrives with object number 255 - a number
; no DDB declares. Both references reserve a full 256-slot object table
; pre-filled with "not created" (jdaad.js:719-725, PCDAAD
; objects.pas:149), so such a condact fails its condition instead of
; faulting.
;
; /PRO 1's first pair is the verbatim shape of URBAN-UPSTART-DEMO.DSF
; /PRO 15's tail, which hung NextDAAD on any unmatched EXAMINE.
/CTL
_
/VOC
EXAMI  35   verb
X      35   verb
TEST   36   verb
BED    147  noun
LAMP   100  noun
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "NULLOBJ PROBE#n"
/1 "You see nothing special."
/OTX
/0 "a lamp"
/LTX
/0 "Arena."
/CON
/0
/OBJ
/0    0   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   LAMP _
; No CLS anywhere: the tilemap leg reads the screen at the prompt, so
; a per-turn clear would wipe the response before it could be read.
/PRO 0
> _ _   PARSE 0
        MES "NOPARSE#n"
> _ _   PROCESS 1
> _ _   REDO
/PRO 1
> X _   WHATO
        NOTEQ @51 255
        PRESENT @51
        MESSAGE 1
        DONE
> X _   SYSMESS 7
        DONE
; The read-only object conditions, each reached with whatever WHATO
; left in flag 51 - object 255 for an unmatched noun.
> TEST _  WHATO
          MES "F51="
          PRINT 51
          MES "#n"
> TEST _  ABSENT @51
          MES "ABSENT#n"
> TEST _  NOTCARR @51
          MES "NOTCARR#n"
> TEST _  NOTWORN @51
          MES "NOTWORN#n"
> TEST _  PRESENT @51
          MES "PRESENT#n"
> TEST _  DONE
/END
